  "term": "ultimatum game",
  "definition": "The ultimatum game is a commonly used bargaining task for studying conflict resolution and decision-making. Researchers use it to examine how responses are shaped by factors such as emotions, personality, cognitive abilities, social norms, power, and perceptions of fairness, reciprocity, and self-interest.",
